From 02e97b9e688d36924f1b6488fc006c5b26125a9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher AMIAUD <christopher.amiaud@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:31:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Emulate fork() with threads on WebAssembly

On hosts without fork(), such as emscripten, fork() failed with
ENOSYS, so a shell could only run its builtins. When threads exist,
HAVE_THREADED_FORK now runs the child process on a new thread, with
its own System holding a copy of the parent's address space, which
non-linear memory makes possible, and a host dup() of each of its
fds. The child keeps its pid across execve(), wait4() reaps it from a
table of children, and a fatal signal only ends that process.

It's only enabled for emscripten so far. MAP_SHARED mappings aren't
shared with the child, they're copied like the rest of its memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
